		"title": "Getting started",
		"icon": "rocket",
		"content": "Vertex Flow brings a keyboard-first task manager into your vault. Projects and\nTasks are plain Markdown notes — you can read and edit them like any other\nnote, and Vertex Flow keeps its own views in sync automatically.\n\n## Install\n\n1. Install **Vertex Flow** from the Community Plugins browser.\n2. (Optional) In **Settings → Vertex Flow**, pick your preferred interface text\n   size — Compact, Cozy, or Comfortable.\n\n## Create a workspace\n\nWorkspaces are the top of the hierarchy and the only mandatory container. You\ncreate one from the **template gallery**, which also copies in example statuses,\npriorities, and types you can shape to your own workflow:\n\n1. From the sidebar's **Workspaces** section, create a new workspace.\n2. Pick a template (appropriate for a solo shopping list all the way up to a\n   full team), give the workspace a name and folder, and choose an ID prefix.\n3. Optionally check **populate with example content** to explore before you\n   build.\n\n## Add your first tasks\n\n1. Add a **Project**, then a **Task** inside it.\n2. Press **Enter** (or open) a task to see its editor — status, priority, type,\n   labels, dates, a description, sub-tasks, and more.\n3. Switch between **List** and **Board** from the view bar above the task list.\n\n## Set up your team and vocabulary\n\nEvery workspace is self-contained. Before you go far, visit **Workspace\nSettings** (`g` `s`) to shape your statuses, priorities, task types, labels,\nand the People register (marking one person as **you** so `assignee:me`\nfilters work).\n\n## Next steps\n\n- Press `?` for the keyboard reference, or open **Help** in the sidebar for the\n  full built-in documentation.\n- Browse the **Concepts** section to understand the model.\n- Build a **Saved View** to pin down the exact view you work from every day.\n- Add a **Dashboard** to watch your progress at a glance."
