				"content": "## Quick capture\n\n**Quick capture** lets you capture a new task without leaving whatever you're\ndoing: run the **Quick capture: new task** command from anywhere in Obsidian\n(command palette or a hotkey), and Vertex Flow creates a task in your most\nrecent workspace and opens it for editing. It's the fastest way to get a\nthought out of your head and into the system.\n\n## Task templates\n\n**Task templates** let you reuse common setups instead of typing them out each\ntime. Templates are defined globally for the workspace, so a \"Bug report\" or\n\"Meeting follow-up\" template can pre-fill a task's fields in one step.\n\n## Bulk actions\n\nWorking with many tasks at once is supported across every list-style view:\n\n- **Select** tasks with `x` (add to selection), `⌘`/`Ctrl` + `a` (select all),\n  or extended arrow selection.\n- **Set status** across the selection from the view bar.\n- **Archive / unarchive** the whole selection with `e`.\n- **Clear filters** to start a selection fresh.\n\nBulk operations act on exactly what you've selected, and archiving — like\ndeleting — never cascades or destroys."
